checks_run.procedure:
Verify the assignment hash, the starting revision and the candidate ID:
- the assignment sha256;
- git rev-parse HEAD, and that the freeze commit differs from the source only in delivery records;
- the candidate ID recomputed in a complete clone and in the repository, at the start and at the end.

Build the candidate:
- an offline frozen-lockfile install from a private copy of the local pnpm store;
- then pnpm -r build;
- then a re-install, to link the built bins.

Run pnpm check:no-cdn. Scan the P4 diff d3e6fe6..dab4562 (diff-scan.sh) for:
- secret-like strings (D4) and remote URLs (D5);
- dynamic code (D6) and raw SQL (D7, D12);
- innerHTML (D8) and float arithmetic on money (D9);
- unsafe sinks in the repair diff (D15).

Run the round-7 unit tests on the confined repository tree, whose node_modules is read-only, with Vitest's --configLoader runner (QA-A's finding):
- session-wait.test.tsx and harness-config.test.ts (unit-web);
- packages/config load.test.ts (unit-node).

Check the root test script and the harness changes.

The root script (FE-R10) must still exit non-zero on any failure:
- execute the EXACT package.json script string with /bin/sh (dash, what pnpm uses here) and a stub vitest first on PATH;
- try all 8 pass/fail combinations of the three projects;
- also try an appended argument, as 'pnpm test <arg>' produces;
- confirm with the real harness run (SEC-R7-07).

The harness changes:
- the unit-web setup.ts warm-up;
- the session-end.spec.ts boot-/me wait;
- the new session-wait test;
- whether CI passes arguments to pnpm test.

Check that supervise-cadence.test.ts catches a regression of F-DG4-128. Apply each mutation, run the test file on a disposable PostgreSQL, then restore with git checkout:
- M0: control, no mutation;
- M1: createBoss stops passing superviseIntervalSeconds;
- M2: main.ts calls createBoss(url) without the configured value;
- M3: the loader drops .max(600).

Re-run the round-2 generated sweep probe S UNCHANGED against this candidate. It covers every P4 operation:
- AUD: 403 on every P4 write, each with exactly one authorization.denied;
- ADM-only and outsider: every write refused, with no transformation-scoped disclosure on any P4 read;
- a scope-limited user: no read discloses another transformation;
- a table checksum identical before and after.

Re-run UNCHANGED:
- the round-1 IDOR probes: foreign ids in paths and bodies through an empty transformation, with a checksum of foreign rows;
- the round-3 drill-down scope probe;
- the round-4 outcome-scope and currency probes;
- the round-5 dashboard filter-scope probe.

Together they cover the dashboard, drill-down, workspace header, KPI outcomes, the Finance and adoption reads, and the server-side scope of client-built transformation lists (ADR-0037 §6).

