checks_run.procedure:
Re-run UNCHANGED:
- round-1 approvals: SoD through a group and through delegation, concurrent approve, approve against withdraw, the delegation loop guard, a stale version;
- round-2 finance: concurrent Finance decisions, stale amend and reverse, never editing a validated value in place, exact decimals, migration 0061;
- round-2 gate-commit: commit-time re-checks;
- round-2 sod-denials and slice-b-ids;
- round-3 and round-4 required-members.

NEW this round, probe H (sec-dg4-r7-handover-race.test.ts):
- H1: four concurrent receiving-owner acceptances;
- H2: accept against return (3 rounds);
- H3: two concurrent returns;
- H4: two concurrent creates for the same area and cycle.

I also read handovers.ts acceptHandover (683-735) and ADR-0034 §SoD.

checks_run.actual:
Re-runs, all exit 0:
- r1-approvals 6/6;
- r2-finance 10/10;
- r2-gate-commit 6/6;
- r2-sod-denials 4/4;
- r2-slice-b-ids 1/1;
- r3-required-members 2/2;
- r4-required-members 2/2.

Probe H, 4/4, exit 0:
- H1: one 200 and three 409 version_conflict; one bau_handover.accept event, one sustainment_review, and the area version 1→2 (bau).
- H2: accept wins twice and return wins once. Each time the loser gets 409 and the end state is consistent: accepted with one review and no return event, or returned with no review and no accept event.
- H3: one 200 and one 409.
- H4: one 201 and one 409 bau_handover.exists; one row.

The code: acceptHandover checks that the caller is the receiving owner before the version (403 bau_handover.not_receiving_owner). It runs under a row lock in one transaction with If-Match, audits the handover and the area, and does no remote I/O.

That the handover's preparer may also be its receiving owner, if they hold both permissions, is a documented decision (ADR-0034 line 180: no SoD beyond this is required by the slice G sources), not a defect.

The integration suites approvals 17, delegations 13, handovers 11, corrections 6 and slice-b-denials 7 pass in both runs.

checks_run.procedure:
